{
  "_comment": "Metalstorm unit-class vocabulary (PLAN-metalstorm-command-language.md §2, M0). The ONE table that maps what a player SAYS to what the sim CALLS things. Keys under `classes` are literal `customparams.ms_class` values — the taxonomy set in data/games/metalstorm/units/_builder.lua (`ms_class = spec.class`) and in the three hand-written families that set ms_class directly (buildings_military.lua / buildings_civilian.lua → \"buildings\", civilians.lua, civvehicles.lua). class-vocabulary.test.ts fails if a key here is not a shipped ms_class, so this file cannot drift from the unit defs the way free-text-accelerator.ts's old hand-kept IDLE_CLASSES did. MERGE NOTE (2026-08-13, nl-command M0-M3 landing): the ten classes the model-integration M1 vehicle roster and M2 sites added on main (balloon, command, courier, expedition, landing_ship, scout, sites, supply, tanker, technical) are grafted in verbatim, and the roles tables are unioned (recon gains scout/balloon matches; logistics/transport kept from main).",
  "_consumers": "Fetched alongside metalstorm.ui.json by widget-loader.ts and handed to free-text-accelerator.ts (the local slot-filler) and the command console. M1+ adds the LLM system prompt, typed autocomplete and the command builder as further consumers of this same file — one vocabulary, many consumers (design pillar 5).",
  "_scales": "`scales` keys are `customparams.ms_scale` values: 1 Light, 2 Line, 3 Heavy, 4 Super-heavy (_builder.lua SCALE_WORDS). Only the classes generated by _builder.lua ship in 4 scales; buildings/civilians/civvehicles are authored one-off and carry no ms_scale, so they declare no `scales`.",
  "_matching": "`display` is singular UI text; `plural` is how the class is normally spoken. `synonyms` and the `scales` phrases are matched case-insensitively, longest phrase first, against the player's words — they are alternative SPELLINGS of the class, never new classes. Keep every phrase lowercase.",
